29,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems that the users of our facilities aren't always satisfied; the reviews suggest that shared, bookable spaces are far more successful than those restricted to a single department.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings confirm a significant demand for general-purpose rooms, while specialist spaces often sit idle, and the cost of replacing rooms out of service has been surprisingly high.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"It appears our technical staff are burdened with manual tasks that should be automated, and we have a concerning number of unfilled grounds and front-of-house positions.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The delivery schedules show a worrying trend where comfort-based projects slip by a year or more, and surveys indicate that hazardous materials in older blocks frequently cause unexpected delays.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The financial data reveals that mechanical and plant costs are rising significantly, while we have failed to set aside any reserves for replacing aging audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Given the preference for bookable spaces and the risks associated with older blocks, we should be cautious about any plan that limits access or involves ground-floor partitions.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,I agree; we must prioritize projects that maximize general utility and minimize the disruption to our existing timetable and budget.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"I believe we should prioritize a plan that reduces the manual burden on our technicians, as the current situation is simply unsustainable for the staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"We must also consider the risk of schedule slippage; any project based on ""comfort"" or located in older blocks could easily be delayed by a year or more.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"We should also be mindful that any project involving mechanical plant will likely exceed previous budget estimates, and we must address the lack of reserves for equipment replacement.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"If we seek a project that is likely to be well-received and manageable, we should avoid those that are overly specialized or prone to the delays Mizuki mentioned.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Victoria,,That suggests we should favor a project that provides high-demand general space without requiring extensive structural changes to the older blocks.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,I must insist that we don't overlook the human element; any plan that fails to alleviate the daily grind of our technicians is a missed opportunity.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree that staff welfare is important, but we must balance that against the high probability of project failure if we ignore the historical data on delays.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a delicate balance, but we must ensure the chosen project is financially viable and doesn't leave us with an unfunded equipment crisis in a few years.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I think we have a clear picture of the risks; we need a project that is bookable, avoids hazardous older partitions, and remains financially predictable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree, and we should specifically look for a project that doesn't force us to hire expensive off-site space to cover for rooms taken out of service.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,George,,"I still believe the most urgent need is to support our staff, particularly those performing manual routines that could be eliminated through better equipment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"We must be realistic about the timeline; if a project is purely for appeal rather than a necessity, we risk another year of slippage.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all searching for a rare unicorn: a project that is high-utility, staff-friendly, and miraculously immune to both inflation and the unpredictability of our old walls.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
