55,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Now that the candidates are before us, the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade seems to address George's concerns about technician routines, though it involves the mechanical plant Benjamin warned about.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"The Central Study Commons aligns perfectly with the need for bookable, general-purpose space and avoids the high costs of off-site room replacement.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade is the only option that directly relieves the manual burden on our technicians, which I believe is our most pressing internal issue.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The Central Study Commons is a comfort-based project in a ground-floor hall, which makes me very concerned about potential hazardous materials and significant schedule slippage.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Media Production Center would address the audiovisual equipment gap I noted, though the Campus Path Network is the only option that seems financially predictable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"While the Path Network is safe, the Central Study Commons offers the high-utility, bookable nature that users clearly prefer, provided we can manage the risks Mizuki mentioned.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"I believe the risk of slippage is a fair concern, but the demand for general study space is an undeniable priority that outweighs the potential for delays.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,I cannot support the Path Network or the Study Commons when our technicians are struggling with outdated equipment; the Ventilation Upgrade is a necessity for our staff's wellbeing.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"I must disagree; the Ventilation Upgrade involves the very mechanical plant costs Benjamin highlighted, and the Study Commons is a recipe for a year-long delay.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"If we are to be pragmatic, the Media Production Center offers a compromise: it provides bookable utility and addresses the equipment void without the extreme risks of the other options.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"The Media Production Center is an intriguing middle ground, as it satisfies the desire for bookable space while avoiding the structural hazards of the ground-floor hall.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I can see the merit in the Media Production Center, as it fulfills the demand for general-purpose utility without the timetable disruptions associated with larger renovations.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,"I still find it difficult to ignore the technicians' plight, but if the other options are financially or temporally impossible, the Media Production Center is a better choice than a path.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,The Media Production Center seems the most viable; it avoids the hazardous ground-floor partitions of the Commons and the volatile mechanical costs of the Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It appears we have reached a rare moment of consensus; the Media Production Center is the most logical choice to satisfy our diverse and conflicting constraints.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I will cast my vote for the Media Production Center, as it balances user demand with a manageable risk profile.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I will also vote for the Media Production Center, as it provides the general-purpose utility we need without excessive disruption.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,George,,"I will vote for the Media Production Center, as it is a more productive use of funds than the paths, even if it doesn't fully solve the technicians' issues.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I will vote for the Media Production Center, as it is the most realistic option to deliver on schedule and within a predictable budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall cast my vote for the Media Production Center as well; it is the most rational solution to our current predicament.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
